 {"ref":"Hotta, arXiv:1101.3954 (2011), QET introductory review; QET first proposed 2008 (PLA 372, 5671; PRD 78, 045006, NAMED-NOT-READ)","effect":"narrows","what":"Confirms that standard teleportation teleports no energy (p.4). Establishes that LOCC on a ground-state-entangled interacting medium extracts E_B > 0 at B with E_B <= E_A, from local zero-point fluctuations. This is a named exception to the tree's unqualified 'no energy moves', and it moves no matter.","read_status":"READ (p.1, 3-6, 12-24, 26-28, 31-40, 41-49)"},
