 {"ref":"Haque, arXiv:2601.18718v1 (2026)","effect":"narrows","what":"For finite-range gapped lattice Hamiltonians with a unique ground state, the energy extractable at distance d is bounded by C e^{-mu d} (eq. 17). This further limits QET's reach. DISCREPANCY, recorded and not repaired: the abstract writes '|E_A - E_B| <= C e^{-mu d}', while the body defines E_B as the post-protocol excess energy and bounds DeltaE := E_A - E_B, the extraction. The two readings differ in notation only. Single-author v1; refereeing status not read.","read_status":"READ (p.1-4)"},
